{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-set-variable","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0085","math_ordinal":81,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH21-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The sentence has just introduced G as an arbitrary measurable upper bound modulo negligible sets.  Its hypothesis must be E setminus G negligible; the conclusion then proves F setminus G negligible and establishes that F is the essential supremum.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt215.tex:105","source_normalized_sha256":"c9e8c5493b74286611c1946b518754e7285cf53768fb26280d7d784865dffaaf","source_text":"$E\\setminus F$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt215.tex:103","target_normalized_sha256":"b12382caa7a50bdfd75b9ededf43a6aa8a549520855e54315f11821d2d4a07ac","target_text":"$E\\setminus G$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S215"}
